---
import Reading from './Reading.astro'

const cases = [
  {
    title: 'Debt collection over WhatsApp, for a multinational agro company',
    body: `Agents used to query invoices and send payment barcodes by hand, one customer at a
    time. Every minute a customer waited, they were more likely to abandon the process
    and buy from a competitor instead. I built a WhatsApp agent that authenticates the
    customer, pulls the invoice in real time, and sends the barcode with no person involved
    at any step. Built on AWS, with Lambda and DynamoDB doing the heavy lifting and Python
    underneath.`,
    reading: {
      pos: '90%',
      left: 'Manual, one at a time',
      right: '~R$4M/day (~US$750K)',
    },
  },
  {
    title: "A sales agent for Brazil's largest car dealership group",
    body: `Leads from the website for BYD and Toyota models were cooling off in the gap between
    form submission and a callback. Across dozens of locations, sales couldn't close that
    gap fast enough. The agent I built picks up the lead the moment the form is submitted,
    moves the conversation to WhatsApp, answers product questions, and books the dealership
    visit. It runs on Azure, with Databricks handling the data layer. I can't stand behind a
    clean conversion number here, since the client had no attribution instrumentation in
    place before this project, but the response-time change itself is real and measured.`,
    plain: {
      headline: 'Hours to seconds',
      sub: 'lead response time, across multiple brands and locations',
    },
  },
  {
    title: 'A CRM-to-warehouse pipeline for Gal Capital',
    body: `The sales team ran entirely on Bitrix24, but nobody could see the funnel by team, by
    broker, or by deal, so leadership was making commission and staffing decisions blind. I
    built a pipeline from Bitrix24 into BigQuery, feeding two dashboards: one operational,
    for day-to-day management, and one executive, for the leadership view. Built on GCP,
    using Cloud Functions, PubSub, and Cloud Scheduler.`,
    plain: {
      headline: 'Two dashboards',
      sub: 'team, broker, and deal-level visibility built from zero',
    },
  },
  {
    title: 'A support chatbot for Hotmart',
    body: `The support menu had no real model for what a bot should own versus hand off to a
    human, so requests just accumulated. I scoped it down deliberately: four features, three
    languages, chosen by what the data said actually mattered, not by what was easiest to
    build.`,
    reading: {
      pos: '75%',
      left: 'No clear ownership model',
      right: '74.5% handled, 43.9% resolved',
    },
  },
]
---

<section class="border-t border-line bg-panel-deep py-20" id="work">
  <div class="max-w-[1040px] mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="text-[clamp(28px,3.6vw,38px)] max-w-[20ch]">Four systems, four leaks that stopped.</h2>

    <div class="flex flex-col mt-[52px]">
      {cases.map((c, i) => (
        <div
          class:list={[
            'border-t border-line py-9 grid grid-cols-1 min-[781px]:grid-cols-[1fr_220px] gap-9',
            i === cases.length - 1 && 'border-b',
          ]}
        >
          <div>
            <h3 class="font-sans font-bold text-[21px] leading-[1.35] max-w-[34ch]">{c.title}</h3>
            <p class="text-[15px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-soft mt-[14px] max-w-[60ch]">{c.body}</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex flex-col justify-center">
            {c.reading ? (
              <Reading pos={c.reading.pos} left={c.reading.left} right={c.reading.right} compact />
            ) : (
              <div class="text-[15px] text-ink font-semibold leading-[1.5]">
                {c.plain?.headline}
                <small class="block font-normal text-ink-soft mt-1 text-[13px]">{c.plain?.sub}</small>
              </div>
            )}
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
